---
title: UNFAIR
summary: Understanding Factors explaining Avoidable hospital admissions Inequalities
peopleSummary: Examined how local health systems can reduce socioeconomic inequalities in avoidable emergency hospital admissions.
status: completed
lead: Dr Sarah Sowden
funder: HEE/NIHR Integrated Clinical Academic Clinical Lectureship
timeframe: 2019–2024
teamMembers:
  - sarah-sowden
researchThemes:
  - healthcare-access
whyItMatters:
  heading: Why this study matters
  body: >-
    Emergency hospital admissions for some conditions can be avoided when people receive effective care early. UNFAIR explored what local health systems in England can do to reduce socioeconomic differences in these admissions.
approach:
  heading: How the study worked
  body: >-
    The study used quantitative and qualitative methods to examine how local areas address inequalities in avoidable emergency hospital admissions and what other areas can learn from their approaches.
---
